# Delete a component that has a wire ATTACHED to one of its ports. The AND gate placed at
# (300,200) has its output end at exactly that anchor, so the wire dragged back to it is a
# real connection, not a wire that happens to be nearby. The gate is then selected with the
# Edit Tool (a press at (280,200) is inside the body and is not a wiring point, so EditTool
# routes it to its select half) and deleted. The wire must survive; the gate must not.
tool	add:AND Gate
click	300	200
tool	wiring
drag	400	200	300	200
tool	edit
click	280	200
key	delete
